      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Single intravenous injections of 30 to 35 mCi (1,110 to 1,295 MBq) of Re-186(Sn)HEDP previously have been shown to result in palliation of painful skeletal metastases from prostate cancer. There are no reports of patients receiving repetitive Re-186(Sn)HEDP therapy. We have followed two such patients who received multiple (five to seven) injections of Re-186(Sn)HEDP at 2-month intervals. Each experienced a sustained decrease in both pain and analgesic intake. The only evident clinical or biochemical toxicity was a mild progressive decline in their total platelet counts."},
